WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.750
Hey, Thoughty2 here.

00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:05.810
Japan is probably the most health-conscious
country in the world.

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:10.420
They have the highest life expectancy, the
most centenarians per capita and they eat

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:11.849
sooo much fish.

00:00:11.849 --> 00:00:17.460
As a country, Japan has gone to extraordinary
lengths to maintain its reputation as the

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:19.150
World’s healthiest place.

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:24.160
For instance, the vast majority of Japanese
companies make their employees do mandatory

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:28.720
exercise for half-an-hour every morning before
they sit down to work.

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:33.610
Studies show this not only helps physical
fitness, but also keeps employees mentally

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:35.550
sound and improves productivity.

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:42.050
But Japan doesn’t have a health craze like
Los Angeles, you won’t find any seaweed

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:43.720
and dust diet-fads here.

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:48.420
A healthy-lifestyle is just a deep-rooted
part of the Japanese Culture.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:55.260
But with the influx of Western fast food Japan’s
healthy outlook is showing signs of crumbling,

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:56.980
under a mountain of melty-plastic-cheese.

00:00:56.980 --> 00:01:04.470
And in a country where only 3% of the population
are overweight, tiny when compared to Australia

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:11.110
at 60%, those few people who are obese, tend
to stick out like a sore thumb.

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:16.790
It’s becoming a major problem, because so
few Japanese are overweight there’s a lot

00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:19.640
of prejudice towards the not-so-small minority.

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:24.700
It’s common for overweight individuals to
be bullied in the workplace and even cast

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:28.909
out of their family, just for packing a few
extra pounds.

00:01:28.909 --> 00:01:34.420
Normally governments combat obesity with hopeless
advertising campaigns and even taxing junk

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:35.420
food.

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:41.640
But Japan went the extra mile and simply made
it illegal to be fat.

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:47.290
In 2008 Japan’s lawmakers passed a law called
the “Metabo Law” which is short for metabolic

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:48.290
syndrome.

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:55.170
You may be watching this thinking Japan has
finally lost it, but the Metabo law isn’t

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:57.770
as extreme as it seems.

00:01:57.770 --> 00:02:00.630
You won’t be locked up just for being overweight.

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:04.130
So what is the punishment for committing the
heinous crime of eating too many cheeseburgers?

00:02:04.130 --> 00:02:05.130
Seppuku?

00:02:05.130 --> 00:02:08.560
No, it’s a bit more complicated than that.

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:14.980
Under the Metabo law every Japanese citizen
between the age of 40 to 75 years-old, that’s

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:21.040
44 per cent of the population, has to have
a mandatory check of their waistline every

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.040
year.

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:28.980
The government states that the legal maximum
waist circumference for men is 35.4 inches,

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:33.120
whereas for women it’s only 31.5 inches.

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:38.040
So this law is basically a massive slap in
the face to guys who like curvy women.

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:43.150
To put these insanely restrictive numbers
into perspective, In Japan it’s considered

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:50.069
gross and illegal to have a waist over 35
inches as a male, whereas the average male

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:54.060
waist size in America is 40 inches.

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:58.489
If during their annual checkup, a citizen
is found to have a larger waistline than the

00:02:58.489 --> 00:03:04.390
government imposed limit, they are required
by law to attend regular counselling sessions,

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:10.090
because you know, according to Japan if you’re
fat it must be because you’re mentally unstable.

00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:15.350
And you have to regularly consult a dietitian
to discuss dietary options.

00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:22.300
Whilst the penalty for individuals focuses
on rehabilitation, there are heavy fines for

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:26.239
companies that don’t follow the guidelines.

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:30.849
Under Metabo law companies are required to
monitor the waistlines and general health

00:03:30.849 --> 00:03:35.580
of all their employees and encourage regular
exercise and a healthy lifestyle.

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:42.030
If a company is found the have employees with
illegal waistlines they must pay heavy fines

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:47.120
to the government until everyone in their
business has shed their excess baggage.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:53.890
In fact, fines for companies can be as high
as $19 million dollars, just because someone

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:55.700
in the office is a greedy bugger.

00:03:55.700 --> 00:04:01.310
To avoid these fines companies have resorted
to handing out so-called “Metabo Towels”

00:04:01.310 --> 00:04:06.110
to all their employees, which is a towel with
a built-in tape measure, so employees can

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:10.010
keep a check on their waistline when they
step out the shower each morning.

00:04:10.010 --> 00:04:13.730
Those crazy Japanese may seem, well, crazy.

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:19.549
But this controversial law has worked, obesity
rates have dropped significantly since its

00:04:19.549 --> 00:04:22.079
inception in 2008.

00:04:22.079 --> 00:04:42.129
Well done Japan, but seriously guys, you didn’t
even have an obesity problem in the first

00:04:42.129 --> 00:04:43.129
place.

00:04:43.129 --> 00:04:43.770
Thanks for watching.

